   713→- Do NOT consider name, gender, age, photo, ethnicity, nationality, location.
   714→
   715→SCORING CONTRACT:
   716→- Scores must follow rubric anchors: 0=absent, 25=weak, 50=moderate, 75=strong, 100=perfect with evidence.
   717→- Evidence REQUIRED for scores >= 75. Cite specific resume content.
   718→- Be honest and precise. Avoid clustering around 50.
   719→
   720→CRITICAL MUST-HAVES (missing ANY = hard_fit false): ${criticalMustHaves || "None specified"}
   721→PREFERRED MUST-HAVES (missing = penalty only): ${preferredMustHaves || "None specified"}
   722→
   723→EVALUATION DIMENSIONS:
   724→${dimensionInstructions}
   725→
   726→Return a JSON object with EXACTLY these fields:
   727→- candidate_name: string
   728→- hard_fit: boolean (false if ANY critical must-have is missing)
   729→- matched_critical_must_haves: string[] (which critical must-haves the candidate has)
   730→- missing_critical_must_haves: string[] (which critical must-haves are missing)
   731→- matched_preferred_must_haves: string[]
   732→- missing_preferred_must_haves: string[]
   733→- category_scores: object where each key is a dimension key, value is {score: 0-100, evidence: [{snippet: string, section: string}], notes: string}
   734→- strengths: string[] (top 3 strengths for this specific role)
   735→- gaps: string[] (top 2 gaps/weaknesses for this specific role)
   736→- interview_questions: string[] (${cfg.num_interview_questions} questions targeting gaps)
   737→- explanation: {summary: string, why_ranked_here: string, key_tradeoffs: string}
   738→- confidence: number 0-100 (based on resume text quality and evidence density)
   739→
   740→Return ONLY valid JSON. No markdown.`;
   741→
   742→  const maxChars = cfg.max_resume_chars;
   743→  const resumeContent = parsedJson
   744→    ? `STRUCTURED RESUME DATA:\n${JSON.stringify(parsedJson).slice(0, maxChars)}\n\nRAW RESUME TEXT:\n${resumeText.slice(0, maxChars / 2)}`
   745→    : `RESUME TEXT:\n${resumeText.slice(0, maxChars)}`;
   746→
   747→  const response = await fetch("https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions", {
   748→    method: "POST",
   749→    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${OPENAI_API_KEY}`, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
   750→    body: JSON.stringify({
